{"title": "Circles (Past Year Questions)", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>&nbsp;A circle is circumscribed on a quadrilateral ABCD. If &angle;DAB = 100&deg;, &angle;ADB = 35&deg; and &angle;CDB =40&deg;, then find the measure of &angle;DBC.&nbsp;</p><p></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABCD &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2327;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;DAB = 100&deg;, &#8736;ADB = 35&deg; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;CDB =40&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;DBC &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["35<sup>o</sup>", "60<sup>o</sup>", "45<sup>o</sup>", "40<sup>o</sup>"], "options_hi": ["35<sup>o</sup>", "60<sup>o</sup>", "45<sup>o</sup>", "40<sup>o</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=279 height=205 id=\"Picture 40\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20111/image110.jpg\"></p><p>In &#916; ADB,</p><p>&#8736; ABD = 180  -  (&#8736; ADB + &#8736; DAB)</p><p>= 180  -  (35 + 100)</p><p>= 45&deg;</p><p>Since quadrilateral ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral.</p><p>So,</p><p>&#8736; ADB + &#8736; CDB + &#8736; ABD + &#8736; DBC = 180</p><p>35 + 40 + 45 + &#8736; DBC = 180</p><p>&#8736; DBC = 180  -  120</p><p>&#8736; DBC = 60&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=279 height=205 id=\"Picture 40\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20111/image110.jpg\"></p><p>In &#916; ADB,</p><p>&#8736; ABD = 180  -  (&#8736; ADB + &#8736; DAB)</p><p>= 180  -  (35 + 100)</p><p>= 45&deg;</p><p>Since quadrilateral ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral.</p><p>So,</p><p>&#8736; ADB + &#8736; CDB + &#8736; ABD + &#8736; DBC = 180</p><p>35 + 40 + 45 + &#8736; DBC = 180</p><p>&#8736; DBC = 180  -  120</p><p>&#8736; DBC = 60&deg;</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the number of common tangents, if r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> = C<sub>1</sub> C<sub>2</sub>. (With usual notations, r<sub>1</sub> &amp; r<sub>2</sub> and C<sub>1</sub> &amp; C<sub>2</sub> are the radii and centres of the two circles.)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> = C<sub>1</sub> C<sub>2 </sub>(&#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2325;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; r<sub>1</sub> &#2324;&#2352; r<sub>2 </sub> &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; C<sub>1</sub> &#2324;&#2352; C<sub>2</sub> &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2349;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1", "0", "3", "4"], "options_hi": ["1", "0", "3", "4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>If <img width=13 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image017.png\">+ <img width=15 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image021.png\"> = <img width=35 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image022.png\">, then there are 3 common tangents (2 direct and 1 transverse) .</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>If <img width=13 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image017.png\">+ <img width=15 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image021.png\"> = <img width=35 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image022.png\">, then there are 3 common tangents (2 direct and 1 transverse) .</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the perimeter of major sector of a circle of radius 12 meters, whose minor sector subtends an angle of 75&deg; at the center.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; 12 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; 75&deg; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2328; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["24 + 5&#960; meters", "24 + 19&#960; meters", "24  -  5&#960; meters", "24  -  19&#960; meters"], "options_hi": ["24 + 5&#960; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "24 + 19&#960; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "24 - 5&#960; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "24 - 19&#960; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Arc length of any sector of a circle which makes angle of &#952; at the centre = 2&#960;r * (&#952;/360)</p><p>Total perimeter of the sector = Arc length + 2 * Radius = 2&#960;r * (&#952;/360) + 2r</p><p>Since minor sector makes an angle of 75&deg; at the centre which means major sector will make angle equal to 360&deg;  -  75&deg; = 285&deg;</p><p>So, perimeter of major sector = 2&#960; * 12 * (285/360) + 2 * 12</p><p>= 19&#960; + 24 meters</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Arc length of any sector of a circle which makes angle of &#952; at the centre = 2&#960;r * (&#952;/360)</p><p>Total perimeter of the sector = Arc length + 2 * Radius = 2&#960;r * (&#952;/360) + 2r</p><p>Since minor sector makes an angle of 75&deg; at the centre which means major sector will make angle equal to 360&deg;  -  75&deg; = 285&deg;</p><p>So, perimeter of major sector = 2&#960; * 12 * (285/360) + 2 * 12</p><p>= 19&#960; + 24 meters</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The radii of two circle are 5 cm and 10 cm and the distance between their centres is 17 cm. Find the length of the transverse common tangent</p>", "q_hi": "&#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 17 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341; &#2313;&#2349;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["9 cm", "8 cm", "6 cm", "7.5 cm"], "options_hi": ["9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "7.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Here R<sub>1</sub>=5 cm</p><p>R<sub>2</sub>=17 cm</p><p>Distance=10 cm</p><p>Formula=L= &radic;(d<sup>2</sup>-(R<sub>1</sub>+R<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>Here (R<sub>1</sub>+R<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup>=15<sup>2</sup>=225</p><p>d<sup>2</sup>=17<sup>2</sup>=289</p><p>so L=&radic;(289-225)=8cm.</p><p>option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here R<sub>1</sub>=5 cm</p><p>R<sub>2</sub>=17 cm</p><p>Distance=10 cm</p><p>Formula=L= &radic;(d<sup>2</sup>-(R<sub>1</sub>+R<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>Here (R<sub>1</sub>+R<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup>=15<sup>2</sup>=225</p><p>d<sup>2</sup>=17<sup>2</sup>=289</p><p>so L=&radic;(289-225)=8cm.</p><p>option (b) is the correct answer.</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A chord of length 42 cm is drawn in a circle having diameter 58 cm. what is the minimum distance of other parallel chord of length 40 cm in the same circle from 42 cm long chord?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>58 cm &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 42 cm &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366; &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 40 cm &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; 42 cm &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["4 cm", "1 cm", "3 cm", "2 cm"], "options_hi": ["4 cm", "1 cm", "3 cm", "2 cm"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=277 height=271 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20787/image029.jpg\"></p><p>Radius = OA = OC = 58/2 = 29 cm</p><p>Chord AB = 42 cm So, AE = 21 cm</p><p>And chord CD = 40 cm So, CF = 20 cm</p><p>OF<sup>2</sup> = OC<sup>2</sup>  -  CF<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; OF = &radic;(841  -  400) = &radic;441</p><p>=&gt; OF = 21 cm</p><p>And OE<sup>2</sup> = OA<sup>2</sup>  -  AE<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; OE = &radic;(841  -  441) = &radic;400</p><p>=&gt; OE = 20 cm</p><p>So, EF = OF  -  OE = 21  -  20 = 1 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=277 height=271 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20787/image029.jpg\"></p><p>Radius = OA = OC = 58/2 = 29 cm</p><p>Chord AB = 42 cm So, AE = 21 cm</p><p>And chord CD = 40 cm So, CF = 20 cm</p><p>OF<sup>2</sup> = OC<sup>2</sup>  -  CF<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; OF = &radic;(841  -  400) = &radic;441</p><p>=&gt; OF = 21 cm</p><p>And OE<sup>2</sup> = OA<sup>2</sup>  -  AE<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; OE = &radic;(841  -  441) = &radic;400</p><p>=&gt; OE = 20 cm</p><p>So, EF = OF  -  OE = 21  -  20 = 1 cm</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two circles of radii 8 cm and 3 cm, respectively, are 13 cm apart. AB is a direct common tangent touch to both the circles at A and B respectively then the length of AB is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 8 cm &#2324;&#2352; 3 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; 13 cm &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; AB &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2368;&#2343;&#2368; &#2313;&#2349;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; AB &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["10 cm", "12 cm", "8 cm", "6 cm"], "options_hi": ["10 cm", "12 cm", "8 cm", "6 cm"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>When two circles of radii r<sub>1</sub> cm and r<sub>2</sub> cm are d cm apart (d &gt; r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> and r<sup>2</sup> &gt; r<sub>1</sub>), then length of their common tangent = &radic;[d<sup>2</sup>  -  (r<sub>2</sub>  -  r<sub>1</sub>)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>AB = &radic;[13<sup>2</sup>  -  (8  -  3)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= &radic;[169  -  25]</p><p>= &radic;144</p><p>= 12 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>When two circles of radii r<sub>1</sub> cm and r<sub>2</sub> cm are d cm apart (d &gt; r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> and r<sup>2</sup> &gt; r<sub>1</sub>), then length of their common tangent = &radic;[d<sup>2</sup>  -  (r<sub>2</sub>  -  r<sub>1</sub>)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>AB = &radic;[13<sup>2</sup>  -  (8  -  3)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= &radic;[169  -  25]</p><p>= &radic;144</p><p>= 12 cm</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Select the correct option with respect to the given statement.</p><p>Two tangents are drawn at the end of the diameter of a circle.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["They intersect each other.", "They pass through origin.", "They are parallel to each other.", "They are perpendicular to each other."], "options_hi": ["&#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;", "&#2357;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2332;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;", "&#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;", "&#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2357;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=270 height=174 id=\"Picture 79\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21889/image056.png\"></p><p><b>We know that:</b> The radius from the center of the circle to the point of tangency is perpendicular to the tangent line.</p><p>&#8736;AMO = &#8736;CNO = 90&deg;</p><p>Hence, two tangents are drawn at the end of the diameter of a circle are parallel to each other.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=270 height=174 id=\"Picture 79\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21889/image056.png\"></p><p><b>We know that:</b> The radius from the center of the circle to the point of tangency is perpendicular to the tangent line.</p><p>&#8736;AMO = &#8736;CNO = 90&deg;</p><p>Hence, two tangents are drawn at the end of the diameter of a circle are parallel to each other.</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a circle of radius 3 cm, two chords of length 2 cm and 3 cm lie on the same side of a diameter. What is the perpendicular distance between the two chords?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>3 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 2 cm &#2324;&#2352; 3 cm &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2323;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2357;&#2340; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["(4&#8730;3 - 3&#8730;2)/2 cm", "(4&#8730;2 - 3&#8730;3)/2 cm", "(4&#8730;2 - 3&#8730;3)/3 cm", "(4&#8730;2 - 3&#8730;3)/4 cm"], "options_hi": ["(4&radic;3 - 3&radic;2)/2 cm", "(4&radic;2 - 3&radic;3)/2 cm", "(4&radic;2 - 3&radic;3)/3 cm", "(4&radic;2 - 3&radic;3)/4 cm"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=205 height=162 id=\"Picture 26\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21007/image100.png\" ></p><p>In &#916; OAM,</p><p>OM<sup>2</sup> = 9  -  (3/2)<sup>2</sup></p><p>OM<sup>2</sup> = 27/4</p><p>OM = 3&radic;3/2 cm</p><p>In &#916; OCN,</p><p>ON<sup>2</sup> = 9  -  1 = 8</p><p>ON = 2&radic;2 cm</p><p>MN = ON  -  OM</p><p>MN = 2&radic;2  -  (3&radic;3/2) cm</p><p>MN = (4&radic;2 - 3&radic;3)/2 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=205 height=162 id=\"Picture 26\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21007/image100.png\" ></p><p>In &#916; OAM,</p><p>OM<sup>2</sup> = 9  -  (3/2)<sup>2</sup></p><p>OM<sup>2</sup> = 27/4</p><p>OM = 3&radic;3/2 cm</p><p>In &#916; OCN,</p><p>ON<sup>2</sup> = 9  -  1 = 8</p><p>ON = 2&radic;2 cm</p><p>MN = ON  -  OM</p><p>MN = 2&radic;2  -  (3&radic;3/2) cm</p><p>MN = (4&radic;2 - 3&radic;3)/2 cm</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the following figure, P and Q are centers of two circles. The circles are intersecting at points A and B. PA produced on both the sides meets the circles at C and D. If &ang;CPB = 100&deg;, then find the value of x.</p><p><img width=208 height=170 id=\"Picture 34\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19993/image024.jpg\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; PA &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2351;&#2361; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; C &#2324;&#2352; D &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;CPB = 100&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; x &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"208\" height=\"170\" id=\"Picture 34\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19993/image024.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["115", "120", "110", "100"], "options_hi": ["115", "120", "110", "100"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=198 height=169 id=\"Picture 33\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19993/image025.jpg\"></p><p>&#8736;CPB = 100&deg;</p><p>&#8736;APB = 180  -  100 = 80&deg;</p><p>In DAPB,</p><p>&#8736;PAB = &ang;PBA = &frac12; (180-80) = 50&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BAD = 180  -  50 = 130&deg;</p><p>In ABED,</p><p>&#8736;BAD + &ang;BED = 180&deg; (In cyclic quadrilateral, the sum of opposite angles is equal to 180&deg;.)</p><p>&#8736;BED = 180&deg; - 130&deg; = 50&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BQD = 2&ang;BED (The angle at the center is double the angle at the circumference.)</p><p>&#8736;BQD = 2 X 50 = 100&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=198 height=169 id=\"Picture 33\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19993/image025.jpg\"></p><p>&#8736;CPB = 100&deg;</p><p>&#8736;APB = 180  -  100 = 80&deg;</p><p>In DAPB,</p><p>&#8736;PAB = &ang;PBA = &frac12; (180-80) = 50&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BAD = 180  -  50 = 130&deg;</p><p>In ABED,</p><p>&#8736;BAD + &ang;BED = 180&deg; (In cyclic quadrilateral, the sum of opposite angles is equal to 180&deg;.)</p><p>&#8736;BED = 180&deg; - 130&deg; = 50&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BQD = 2&ang;BED (The angle at the center is double the angle at the circumference.)</p><p>&#8736;BQD = 2 X 50 = 100&deg;</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>AB is a chord of a circle in minor segment with center O. C is a point on the minorarc of the circle between the points A and B. The tangents to the circle at A and B meet at the point P. If &#8736;ACB = 102&deg;, then what is the measure of &#8736;APB?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>AB, &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; O &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369; &#2330;&#2366;&#2346; &#2346;&#2352; C &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; P &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;ACB = 102&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;APB &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["29&#730;", "27&#730;", "23&#730;", "24&#730;"], "options_hi": ["29&#730;", "27&#730;", "23&#730;", "24&#730;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>&#8736;ACB = 102&#730;</p><p>&#8736;ADB = 180&#730;  -  102&#730; = 78&#730;</p><p>&#8736;AOB = 2 * 78&#730; = 156&#730;</p><p><img width=169 height=211 id=\"Picture 34\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21087/image035.jpg\"></p><p>Since A and B are tangents then</p><p>&#8736;OAP = OBP = 90&#730;</p><p>&#8736;APB = 180&#730; -  156&#730;</p><p>&#8736;APB = 24&#730;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&#8736;ACB = 102&#730;</p><p>&#8736;ADB = 180&#730;  -  102&#730; = 78&#730;</p><p>&#8736;AOB = 2 * 78&#730; = 156&#730;</p><p><img width=169 height=211 id=\"Picture 34\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21087/image035.jpg\"></p><p>Since A and B are tangents then</p><p>&#8736;OAP = OBP = 90&#730;</p><p>&#8736;APB = 180&#730; -  156&#730;</p><p>&#8736;APB = 24&#730;</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The area of the sector of a circle is 128 sq. cm. If the length of the arc of that sector is 64 cm, then find the radius of the circle.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 128 sq. cm. &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 64 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4 cm", "8 cm", "2 cm", "16 cm"], "options_hi": ["4 cm", "8 cm", "2 cm", "16 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the radius of the circle be 'r' cm.</p><p>Since, the area of the sector = 128 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>And the length of the arc of that sector = 64 Cm</p><p>So,</p><p>r/2 * 64 = 128</p><p>r = 4 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the radius of the circle be 'r' cm.</p><p>Since, the area of the sector = 128 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>And the length of the arc of that sector = 64 Cm</p><p>So,</p><p>r/2 * 64 = 128</p><p>r = 4 cm</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three circles of radius 7 cm are kept touching each other. The string is tightly tied around these three circles. What is the length of the string?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>7 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2352;&#2326;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2311;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342; &#2327;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342; &#2319;&#2325; &#2337;&#2379;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2360;&#2325;&#2352; &#2348;&#2305;&#2343;&#2368; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2337;&#2379;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["42 + 7p cm", "21p + 14 cm", "42 + 14p cm", "7 + 14p cm"], "options_hi": ["42 + 7p cm", "21p + 14 cm", "42 + 14p cm", "7 + 14p cm"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=224 height=184 id=\"Picture 29\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image018.jpg\"></p><p>r = 7 cm</p><p>The length of the string = Length of string not in contact with circle + Length of string in contact with circle</p><p>= (3 * 2r) + 3 * <img width=28 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image019.png\"></p><p>= (3 * 14) + 3 * <img width=31 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image020.png\"></p><p>= (42 + 14&#960;) or (42 + 14p)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=224 height=184 id=\"Picture 29\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image018.jpg\"></p><p>r = 7 cm</p><p>The length of the string = Length of string not in contact with circle + Length of string in contact with circle</p><p>= (3 * 2r) + 3 * <img width=28 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image019.png\"></p><p>= (3 * 14) + 3 * <img width=31 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image020.png\"></p><p>= (42 + 14&#960;) or (42 + 14p)</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Chords AB and CD of a circle intersect externally at P. If AB = 7 cm, CD = 1 cm and PD = 5 cm, then 50% of the length of PA (in cm) is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305;- AB &#2324;&#2352; CD &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2351; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; P &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; AB = 7 cm, CD = 1 cm &#2324;&#2352; PD = 5 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; PA &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; 50% (cm &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["5", "10", "8", "3"], "options_hi": ["5", "10", "8", "3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=282 height=173 id=\"Picture 59\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20002/image069.png\"></p><p>Let PB = 'x' cm</p><p><b>We know that: </b>PA * PB = PC * PD</p><p>(x + 7) * x = (5 + 1) * 5</p><p>x (x + 7) = 30 = 3 * (3 + 7)</p><p>After comparing:</p><p>x = 3</p><p>PA = x + 7 = 10 cm</p><p>50% of PA = 5 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=282 height=173 id=\"Picture 59\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20002/image069.png\"></p><p>Let PB = 'x' cm</p><p><b>We know that: </b>PA * PB = PC * PD</p><p>(x + 7) * x = (5 + 1) * 5</p><p>x (x + 7) = 30 = 3 * (3 + 7)</p><p>After comparing:</p><p>x = 3</p><p>PA = x + 7 = 10 cm</p><p>50% of PA = 5 cm</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Let O is the centre of a circle and P is a point outside the circle. If PAB is a secant of the circle which intersects the circle at A and B, and PT is the tangent drawn from P, then find the length of PT. [PA = 3 cm and AB = 9 cm]</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; O &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; P &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; PAB &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2331;&#2375;&#2342;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;/&#2360;&#2368;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; PAB &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; PT, P &#2360;&#2375; &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; PT &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; [PA = 3 cm &#2324;&#2352; AB = 9 cm]</p>", "options_en": ["8 cm", "4 cm", "10 cm", "6 cm"], "options_hi": ["8 cm", "4 cm", "10 cm", "6 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=268 height=192 id=\"Picture 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20927/image066.png\"></p><p>Given: PA = 3 cm and AB = 9 cm</p><p>PB = PA + AB = 3 + 9 = 12 cm</p><p>We know that:</p><p>PT<sup>2</sup> = PA * PB</p><p>PT<sup>2</sup> = 3 * 12 = 36</p><p>PT = 6 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=268 height=192 id=\"Picture 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20927/image066.png\"></p><p>Given: PA = 3 cm and AB = 9 cm</p><p>PB = PA + AB = 3 + 9 = 12 cm</p><p>We know that:</p><p>PT<sup>2</sup> = PA * PB</p><p>PT<sup>2</sup> = 3 * 12 = 36</p><p>PT = 6 cm</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>PA and PB are two tangents from a point P outside the circle with center O. If A and B are points on the circle such that &#8736;APB = 128&deg;, then &#8736;OAB is equal to:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>PA &#2324;&#2352; PB &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; O &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; P &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2320;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; &#8736;APB = 128&deg;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;OAB &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;:</p>", "options_en": ["38&deg;", "64&deg;", "72&deg;", "52&deg;"], "options_hi": ["38&deg;", "64&deg;", "72&deg;", "52&deg;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=268 height=153 id=\"Picture 24\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image091.png\"></p><p>&#8736;APB = 128&deg;</p><p>In Quadrilateral PAOB:</p><p>&#8736;APB + &#8736;AOB = 180&deg; [&#8736;PAO = &#8736;PBO = 90&deg; = Angle formed between tangent and radius.]</p><p>&#8736;AOB = 180&deg; - 128&deg; = 52&deg;</p><p>In &#916;AOB:</p><p>&#8736;AOB + &#8736;OAB + &#8736;OBA = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;OAB + &#8736;OAB = 180&deg; - 52&deg; = 128&deg; [&#8736;OAB = &#8736;OBA]</p><p>&#8736;OAB = 128&deg;/2 = 64&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=268 height=153 id=\"Picture 24\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image091.png\"></p><p>&#8736;APB = 128&deg;</p><p>In Quadrilateral PAOB:</p><p>&#8736;APB + &#8736;AOB = 180&deg; [&#8736;PAO = &#8736;PBO = 90&deg; = Angle formed between tangent and radius.]</p><p>&#8736;AOB = 180&deg; - 128&deg; = 52&deg;</p><p>In &#916;AOB:</p><p>&#8736;AOB + &#8736;OAB + &#8736;OBA = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;OAB + &#8736;OAB = 180&deg; - 52&deg; = 128&deg; [&#8736;OAB = &#8736;OBA]</p><p>&#8736;OAB = 128&deg;/2 = 64&deg;</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A circle is inscribed in a triangle ABC. It touches sides AB, BC and AC at points R, P and Q, respectively. If AQ = 3.5 cm, PC = 4.5 cm and BR = 7 cm, then the perimeter (in cm) of the triangle &#916;ABC is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2361; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; AB, BC &#2324;&#2352; AC &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; R, P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; AQ = 3.5 cm, PC = 4.5 cm &#2324;&#2352; BR = 7 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#916;ABC &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; (cm &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["45", "15", "28", "30"], "options_hi": ["45", "15", "28", "30"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=216 height=167 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image090.png\"></p><p>AQ = 3.5 cm, PC = 4.5 cm and BR = 7 cm</p><p>AQ = AR = 3.5 cm, PC = QC = 4.5 cm, and BP = BR = 7 cm</p><p>Perimeter of the triangle = AB + BC + AC = (AR + BR) + (BP + PC) + (AQ + QC) = 2 * (3.5 + 4.5 + 7)</p><p>= 2 * 15</p><p>= 30 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=216 height=167 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image090.png\"></p><p>AQ = 3.5 cm, PC = 4.5 cm and BR = 7 cm</p><p>AQ = AR = 3.5 cm, PC = QC = 4.5 cm, and BP = BR = 7 cm</p><p>Perimeter of the triangle = AB + BC + AC = (AR + BR) + (BP + PC) + (AQ + QC) = 2 * (3.5 + 4.5 + 7)</p><p>= 2 * 15</p><p>= 30 cm</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two circles touch each other externally. The radius of the first circle with center A is 18 cm. The radius of the second circle with center B is 8 cm. Find the length of their common tangent CD.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2351; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; A &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; B &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2313;&#2349;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; CD &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["23 cm", "26 cm", "24 cm", "25 cm"], "options_hi": ["23 cm", "26 cm", "24 cm", "25 cm"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><b>We know that:</b> When two circles of radius r<sub>1</sub> and r<sub>2</sub> touches each other externally, then length of their common tangent = 2&radic;r<sub>1</sub>r<sub>2</sub></p><p>Length of the common tangent = 2&radic;(18 * 8) = 2&radic;144</p><p>= 2 * 12</p><p>= 24 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>We know that:</b> When two circles of radius r<sub>1</sub> and r<sub>2</sub> touches each other externally, then length of their common tangent = 2&radic;r<sub>1</sub>r<sub>2</sub></p><p>Length of the common tangent = 2&radic;(18 * 8) = 2&radic;144</p><p>= 2 * 12</p><p>= 24 cm</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the given figure, MNP, SQP, NQR and MSR are straight lines. &#8736;NPQ = 54&deg; and = &#8736;QRS = 68&deg;. What is the degree measure of &#8736;SMN?</p><p><img width=339 height=272 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22631/image093.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, MNP, SQP, NQR &#2324;&#2352; MSR &#2360;&#2368;&#2343;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#8736;NPQ = 54&deg; &#2324;&#2352; = &#8736;QRS = 68&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#8736;SMN &#2325;&#2366; &#2337;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"339\" height=\"272\" id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22631/image093.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["29&deg;", "38&deg;", "54&deg;", "68&deg;"], "options_hi": ["29&deg;", "38&deg;", "54&deg;", "68&deg;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>In &#916;MNR:</p><p>&#8736;MNR + &#8736;RMN + &#8736;MRN = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;MNR + &#8736;RMN = 180&deg; - 68&deg; = 112&deg;</p><p>&#8736;MNR + &#8736;SMN = 112&deg; .......... (1)</p><p>In &#916;SMP:</p><p>&#8736;SMP + &#8736;MSP + &#8736;SPM = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;SMP + &#8736;MSP = 180&deg; - 54&deg; = 126&deg;</p><p>&#8736;SMN + &#8736;MSP = 126&deg; ........ (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>(&#8736;MNR + &#8736;SMN) + (&#8736;SMN + &#8736;MSP) = 112&deg; + 126&deg;</p><p>(&#8736;MNR + &#8736;MSP) + (&#8736;SMN + &#8736;SMN) = 238&deg;</p><p>(&#8736;MNR + &#8736;MSP) + 2(&#8736;SMN) = 238&deg; ....... (3)</p><p>In cyclic quadrilateral SMNQ:</p><p>&#8736;MSQ + &#8736;MNQ = 180&deg; ........... (4)</p><p>From (3) and (4):</p><p>180&deg; + 2(&#8736;SMN) = 238&deg;</p><p>&#8736;SMN = 29&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In &#916;MNR:</p><p>&#8736;MNR + &#8736;RMN + &#8736;MRN = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;MNR + &#8736;RMN = 180&deg; - 68&deg; = 112&deg;</p><p>&#8736;MNR + &#8736;SMN = 112&deg; .......... (1)</p><p>In &#916;SMP:</p><p>&#8736;SMP + &#8736;MSP + &#8736;SPM = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;SMP + &#8736;MSP = 180&deg; - 54&deg; = 126&deg;</p><p>&#8736;SMN + &#8736;MSP = 126&deg; ........ (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>(&#8736;MNR + &#8736;SMN) + (&#8736;SMN + &#8736;MSP) = 112&deg; + 126&deg;</p><p>(&#8736;MNR + &#8736;MSP) + (&#8736;SMN + &#8736;SMN) = 238&deg;</p><p>(&#8736;MNR + &#8736;MSP) + 2(&#8736;SMN) = 238&deg; ....... (3)</p><p>In cyclic quadrilateral SMNQ:</p><p>&#8736;MSQ + &#8736;MNQ = 180&deg; ........... (4)</p><p>From (3) and (4):</p><p>180&deg; + 2(&#8736;SMN) = 238&deg;</p><p>&#8736;SMN = 29&deg;</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral such that AB is a diameter of the circle circumscribing it and &#8736;ADC = 118&deg;, What is the measure of &#8736;BAC?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>ABCD &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; AB &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2327;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;ADC = 118&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;BAC &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["32&deg;", "28&deg;", "45&deg;", "30&deg;"], "options_hi": ["32&deg;", "28&deg;", "45&deg;", "30&deg;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=226 height=167 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22634/image116.png\"></p><p>In the cyclic quadrilateral ABCD:</p><p>&#8736;ADC + &#8736;ABC = &#8736;DAB + &#8736;DCB = 180&deg;</p><p>Since, &#8736;ADC = 118&deg;</p><p>So, &#8736;ABC = 180  -  118 = 62&deg;</p><p>In triangle OBC:</p><p>OB = OC</p><p>So, &#8736;OBC = &#8736;OCB</p><p>Since, &#8736;OBC = &#8736;ABC = 62&deg;</p><p>So, &#8736;OCB = 62&deg;</p><p>And, &#8736;BOC = 180  -  (62 + 62) = 56&deg;</p><p>Since, &#8736;BOC = 2&#8736;BAC</p><p>So, &#8736;BAC = 56/2 = 28&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=226 height=167 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22634/image116.png\"></p><p>In the cyclic quadrilateral ABCD:</p><p>&#8736;ADC + &#8736;ABC = &#8736;DAB + &#8736;DCB = 180&deg;</p><p>Since, &#8736;ADC = 118&deg;</p><p>So, &#8736;ABC = 180  -  118 = 62&deg;</p><p>In triangle OBC:</p><p>OB = OC</p><p>So, &#8736;OBC = &#8736;OCB</p><p>Since, &#8736;OBC = &#8736;ABC = 62&deg;</p><p>So, &#8736;OCB = 62&deg;</p><p>And, &#8736;BOC = 180  -  (62 + 62) = 56&deg;</p><p>Since, &#8736;BOC = 2&#8736;BAC</p><p>So, &#8736;BAC = 56/2 = 28&deg;</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the given figure, the length of arc AB is equal to twice the length of radius r of the circle. Find the area of sector OAB in terms of the radius r.</p><p><img width=209 height=212 id=\"Picture 50\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image081.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2330;&#2366;&#2346; AB &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; (r) &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; OAB &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; r &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"209\" height=\"212\" id=\"Picture 50\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image081.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["3r", "2r", "&#960;r<sup>2</sup>", "r<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["3r", "2r", "&#960;r<sup>2</sup>", "r<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Length of arc = 2r</p><p><b>We know that: </b>Angle = Arc/Radius</p><p>Angle (&#952;) = 2r/r</p><p>&#952; = 2</p><p>Now,</p><p>Area of sector of circle = &#960;r<sup>2</sup> * (&#952;/360&deg;)</p><p>= &#960;r<sup>2</sup> * (2/360&deg;)</p><p>= &#960;r<sup>2</sup> * (1/180&deg;) [&#960; = 180&deg;]</p><p>=&#960;r<sup>2</sup> * (1/&#960;)</p><p>= r<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Length of arc = 2r</p><p><b>We know that: </b>Angle = Arc/Radius</p><p>Angle (&#952;) = 2r/r</p><p>&#952; = 2</p><p>Now,</p><p>Area of sector of circle = &#960;r<sup>2</sup> * (&#952;/360&deg;)</p><p>= &#960;r<sup>2</sup> * (2/360&deg;)</p><p>= &#960;r<sup>2</sup> * (1/180&deg;) [&#960; = 180&deg;]</p><p>=&#960;r<sup>2</sup> * (1/&#960;)</p><p>= r<sup>2</sup></p>"}]}